Hi!

The obligations of producers of electrical and electronic equipment (EEE), producers of batteries and portable accumulators (B&A) resulting from the products they introduce to the market, are carried out:

a) *individually*;

b) *through a legal entity* authorised by the supervisory committee of extended liability of producers. 

The *Organisations for the implementation of extended producer responsibility* are the ones that undertake the obligation to reach the recycling targets, and usually reaching the recycling targets is possible by contracting specialised collectors who can prove, through traceability documents, the recycling of equipment waste and those of batteries for the categories that the beneficiary needs. Reporting to these organisations is done monthly by economic agents.

In order to introduce EEE and B&A on the national market, *producers/importers have the obligation to register in the National Register of Electrical and Electronic Equipment Producers, respectively the National Register of Battery and Accumulator Producers within the National Environmental Protection Agency*. 

In the event that there is no contract for handing over responsibility with an Organisation for the Implementation of Extended Producer Responsibility and the quantities of equipment and batteries are declared directly to the AFM - Administration of the Environment Fund fulfilling the obligations individually, the producer/importer has the obligation of annual reporting - to Environmental Protection Agency. 



This domain is covered by many laws, ordinances and orders, but there are many consulting companies in this field in Romania that can advise.

Fortunately, some of these consulting companies have made a summary of the legislation on their websites, like [+here+|https://wastebill.ro/obligatiile-producatorilor-si-importatorilor/]:



According to the legislation in force, the *Producer* is not only the company that manufactures the respective products, but *anyone who places on the national market products that will later become specially regulated waste*, such as:

* electrical and electronic equipment - EEE;
* batteries and accumulators – B&A;
* tires;
* oils and lubricants



Obligations of producers:

* *the organisation of the extended producer liability system (individually or through a collective organisation* that ensures the fulfilment of the extended producer liability);
* preparation of *monthly records*:
* monthly reporting of the quantities introduced on the national market to the contracted collective organisation;
* the monthly declaration to the Environment Fund Administration of the quantities of specially regulated products introduced on the national market and for which there is an obligation to declare (packaging, electrical and electronic equipment, batteries and accumulators, oils, tires, environmentally hazardous substances, etc.) as well as the quantities of recovered or collected waste, as the case may be;
* annual reports to the county agencies for environmental protection, as well as to the National Agency for Environmental Protection;



*The obligations of electrical and electronic equipment producers* (and implicitly importers) are:

# _Registration in the National Register of Electrical and Electronic Equipment Producers administered by the National Environmental Protection Agency, in order to obtain the Registration Number (licence) that allows the introduction of electrical and electronic equipment into the national territory_.

* Before introducing any electrical or electronic equipment to the national market, producers have the obligation to check whether they fall under GEO 5/2015 and to register in the National Register of Electrical and Electronic Equipment Producers, within the National Agency for Protection Environment, in order to obtain the Registration Number.



# _Management of electrical and electronic equipment from own production, intra-community purchase or import, in accordance with the dedicated normative acts_

* In this sense, the producer has the obligation to draw up a monthly management of the equipment introduced on the national market, which requires the correct identification of the type of equipment and its weight (without the related packaging and without batteries, if they are incorporated in the equipment), categorization and submission of mandatory reports to the competent authorities.



# _Mandatory reporting for producers or importers of electrical and electronic equipment_

* monthly reporting – to the collective organisation contracted for the previous month;
* the monthly statement – to the Environmental Fund;
* annual reporting – to the National Agency for Environmental Protection.



*Obligations of producers for batteries and accumulators (B&A) introduced in Romania*

# Registration in the National Register of Battery and Accumulator Producers administered by the National Environmental Protection Agency in order to obtain the Registration Number (licence) for the introduction of batteries and accumulators into the national territory



# Management of batteries and accumulators from own production, intra-community purchase or import, in accordance with the dedicated normative acts

* As in the case of electrical and electronic equipment, manufacturers of batteries and accumulators have the obligation to draw up a monthly management and to submit the mandatory periodic reports to the competent authorities.



# Mandatory reporting for manufacturers or importers of batteries and accumulators

* monthly reporting – to the collective organisation contracted for the previous month;
* the monthly statement – to the Environmental Fund;
* annual reporting – to the National Agency for Environmental Protection.





In addition to the obligation to establish an extended liability system, *producers have certain fiscal obligations to the Environmental Fund*.



Sorina

