Hi [~accountid:60bd1ba800bdd900683be5fd] 

I appreciate it has been a while, but I’m following up on this issue.

As the only applicable legal basis for this process is legitimate interest, under GDPR  it is mandatory to have the legal analysis of such processing documented. I’m attaching the legitimate interest assessment to this ticket.

The summary, the legal analysis is as follows:

* the processing is permissible and lawful and can be carried out based on legitimate interest, therefore the legal basis required under GDPR is secured;
* currently our Privacy Notice includes sufficient information that the delivery route information may be used for analytical purposes, therefore no changes to this document are need;
* in order to deliver on the rights of the data subjects, following exclusions from the data used for this project should be made:
** data from closed accounts should not be taken into account;
** if our user reaches out and objects to such processing, their data should be also excluded from the processing. Please note that although such requests are very rare, they may be raised and we should be able to deliver on those.



[^Legitimate Interests Assessment (LIA) - Entrance Detection.pdf]

