Hey Sintija,

{quote}how well we inform the rider of the realistic possibilities of getting back their item and how this process is going;{quote}

Yes, I totally agree with you that this is our dark spot, because we actually don’t know what is the possibility of getting the item back and it really depends on the driver. If we would inform the rider about the realistic possibility, we would probably have to tell them, that “you will get your item if the driver will decide to answer back” 😏 That’s the reason why our CSAT drops, because our riders expect us to help them right away, but we can’t do anything without drivers cooperation. And as mentioned previously - we don’t have a way to force the driver to answer us. 

{quote}how well both parties are able to communicate with each other and coordinate the retrieval of the item.{quote}

The language barrier issue in Lithuania is huge, [~accountid:5d95f00136d2520dde7ede17] maybe could jump in here and explain, how many foreign drivers we have right now and what is the scope of the issue. Also, asking the driver to communicate in a written format (via SMS) wouldn’t solve the problem, because again - we can’t be sure that driver will actually send that SMS, and the rider will keep waiting for our support (and creating additional contacts for us).

{quote}Could you tell me more about how the 85% CSAT target for this issue was determined?{quote}

We don't set separate CSAT targets per ATIs, rather we set a general goal for the market and then we target separate ATIs that decrease CSAT the most, to improve the overall result. 85% is the overall goal for the CSAT, for every ATI. 



