{quote}The original requested throughput was for batched data, I’m curious if we publish data record by record, how the Kafka costs will change.{quote}

It’s cents, maybe a couple of dollars per month. Main difference there will be additional TCP/IP headers to transfer for each data packet. But from kafka performance side it’s highly desirable to use batching.

{quote}We would have approximately same total storage, with a 3.7M requests/minute.{quote}

Very rough estimation on differences between single vs batch:

total_amount_of_requests * 40 (some very average size of TCP/IP headers) / 1073741824 (to get size in GB)

Traffic price is $0.01 per GB.



